1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,770
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:03,410
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:08,350
Hyun Jae.

5
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:09,910
Hey, no way.

6
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,620
- It's been a while.
- Good to see you.

7
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,890
- Where are you headed?
- Home.

8
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,790
- Really?
- Have you had dinner?

9
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:49,650
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable.

10
00:00:49,690 --> 00:00:52,120
Please leave a message
after the tone.

11
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:17,120
Seriously, Attorney Seo?

12
00:01:21,890 --> 00:01:23,790
Why aren't you answering my calls?

13
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:32,960
You said you were on call
round the clock for free.

14
00:01:38,970 --> 00:01:41,140
Isn't this a clear neglect of duty?

15
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:48,480
What kind of Daddy Long Legs
behaves like this?

16
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:18,780
Attorney Seo.

17
00:02:21,110 --> 00:02:23,010
I will uncover the truth,
no matter what.

18
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:28,820
Even the injustice
surrounding your death...

19
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:31,790
I will uncover it all.

20
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:38,130
So just trust me.

21
00:02:41,530 --> 00:02:43,670
Just like how I trusted
only you, Attorney Seo.

22
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:49,070
Did Chief Cha say anything today?

23
00:02:50,070 --> 00:02:52,510
Are you two getting engaged or not?

24
00:02:53,310 --> 00:02:55,110
I think we can pick a date.

25
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:57,320
I was able to convince Ms. Park.

26
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:59,880
Hold on.
Did So Yeon happily agree to it?

27
00:03:00,290 --> 00:03:03,490
Yes, I told her that getting engaged
to me would make Seok Jin happy.

28
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:05,190
To that, she immediately agreed.

29
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:07,690
You know how simple-minded she is.

30
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:10,860
Still, she's going to be
your mother-in-law.

31
00:03:10,930 --> 00:03:13,200
You shouldn't talk about her
like that.

32
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:15,670
You need to show her
respect first...

33
00:03:15,730 --> 00:03:17,740
if you want to be loved
as a daughter-in-law.

34
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,740
What do you know
about being a daughter-in-law, Mom?

35
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:22,210
You've never had a mother-in-law.

36
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:25,080
I can't believe you'd say that.

37
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:28,950
Well, I couldn't play the part
even if I wanted to.

38
00:03:29,510 --> 00:03:31,350
If your dad's mom had been alive,

39
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:33,790
I would've been great at it.

40
00:03:34,050 --> 00:03:37,220
Even if it is just an engagement,
we still need to do things properly.

41
00:03:38,290 --> 00:03:39,720
Since you'll be busy,

42
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:44,230
Director Joo should see
if So Yeon needs anything.

43
00:03:45,530 --> 00:03:48,130
- Yes, sir.
- That should be my job.

44
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,600
No matter how busy I am,

45
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:54,240
handling these things personally
is basic courtesy to our in-laws.

46
00:03:55,910 --> 00:03:58,410
Then Director Joo
can accompany you...

47
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:01,310
just in case
there's something you might miss.

48
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:04,150
Sure, I'll adjust my schedule.

49
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:14,590
Dad, hurry out.
I told you I'm in a rush.

50
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:16,690
Hey, I'm out.

51
00:04:16,930 --> 00:04:19,600
Because of you,
I couldn't finish, you punk.

52
00:04:20,670 --> 00:04:21,900
I told you I'm in a rush.

53
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:23,100
Darn it.

54
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:26,040
Why is it so loud
so early in the morning?

55
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:28,240
Well, he's apparently in a rush...

56
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,740
so that he can drop Teun Teun off
at kindergarten.

57
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:31,980
What?

58
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:35,480
Darn. I told you before.

59
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:37,050
Stop caring about
that family's business.

60
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:40,420
Are you her husband
or the kid's father?

61
00:04:40,690 --> 00:04:43,550
Why do you keep hovering
around that woman?

62
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:47,130
Just drop it already.
It's not like anyone is forcing him.

63
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,690
This is what he wants.

64
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:52,700
You know Eun Guk always does
the opposite of what he's told.

65
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:54,500
If you try and stop him,

66
00:04:54,570 --> 00:04:56,830
Eun Guk will only want
to do it more.

67
00:04:57,100 --> 00:05:00,300
As his father, this is what you do
instead of stopping him?

68
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,740
I'm doing this
even if you try to stop me.

69
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:07,880
I'm going to take care of my boss.

70
00:05:08,810 --> 00:05:11,980
What if nasty rumors
get around the neighborhood?

71
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:13,220
It's not a rumor.

72
00:05:13,950 --> 00:05:14,950
What?

73
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:18,460
The more I think about it,
the more I realize it's true.

74
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:20,790
What is? What's the truth?

75
00:05:21,690 --> 00:05:24,100
I have romantic feelings
for my boss.

76
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,460
Mother.

77
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,470
Hey, you punk.

78
00:05:27,470 --> 00:05:30,440
Must you drop a bomb like that
before breakfast?

79
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,170
You're making
your grandmother's blood sugar drop.

80
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:34,070
So don't try to stop me.

81
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:37,110
If you do, I'll pack my bags
and move into her house.

82
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:41,650
I have lived way too long.

83
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,510
Way too long.

84
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:46,220
Mom, should I go get you
some sugar water?

85
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:47,750
Useless idiot!

86
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:50,020
This is all your fault.

87
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,020
How is this my fault?

88
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:54,890
It's not like I played matchmaker
for those two.

89
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:57,100
Forget it. Just forget it!

90
00:05:58,530 --> 00:05:59,630
Unbelievable.

91
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:05,540
Teun Teun,
say you're off like a brave boy.

92
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:09,140
Mom, I'm off.

93
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:11,540
Okay, have a good day.

94
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,280
Let's go.

95
00:06:14,010 --> 00:06:15,010
Eun Guk.

96
00:06:17,850 --> 00:06:18,850
Thank you.

97
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:20,220
Don't mention it.

98
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:22,950
I'll drop Teun Teun off
and open up the cafe.

99
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:33,400
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

100
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:35,500
You should've taken
a few more days off.

101
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:38,740
You still don't look so well.

102
00:06:39,570 --> 00:06:41,270
No, I'm fine.

103
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:43,670
You don't need to put on
a brave face.

104
00:06:45,110 --> 00:06:47,810
I know exactly
what Mr. Seo meant to you.

105
00:06:49,350 --> 00:06:50,620
He told me, you see.

106
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:53,220
He said he'd protect you forever.

107
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:56,590
What good is that promise...

108
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:59,390
when he left me so suddenly?

109
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:02,430
I'll help you.

110
00:07:04,730 --> 00:07:07,100
I'll help you with anything
in his place,

111
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:09,730
so let me know
if you ever need my help.

112
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,570
What if something bad happens
to you too?

113
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:18,140
It won't.

114
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:19,940
It's fine.

115
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,880
I appreciate the thought, though.
I'll get going.

116
00:07:27,990 --> 00:07:29,720
(The Three Women Leading Cheongma)

117
00:07:29,790 --> 00:07:31,790
(Kim Jung Sun, Joo Mi Ran,
and Kang Hae Ra)

118
00:07:53,950 --> 00:07:56,180
Hey. Mr. Choi, you're here.

119
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,050
You should take it easy.

120
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:02,720
How can I when I'm freeloading?
I do have a conscience, you know.

121
00:08:02,990 --> 00:08:06,120
That being said, I'm going to look
for part-time jobs around here.

122
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:14,570
Are you kidding me?

123
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:20,610
Why would you...

124
00:08:21,610 --> 00:08:23,070
look for a job?

125
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:24,980
Why?

126
00:08:28,350 --> 00:08:29,550
I mean,

127
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:33,120
all you need to do
is eat, rest, and relax...

128
00:08:34,590 --> 00:08:36,390
while staying quietly
tucked away in here.

129
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:40,260
Right, I should.

130
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:43,430
It seems shameless, that's all.

131
00:08:43,830 --> 00:08:46,230
Do I really deserve
to sleep in a warm bed...

132
00:08:46,530 --> 00:08:48,670
and eat hot meals
without doing any work?

133
00:08:49,470 --> 00:08:50,600
If you really feel that way,

134
00:08:51,470 --> 00:08:53,000
you can just pay back the favor.

135
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:56,840
How could I possibly pay it back?

136
00:08:58,040 --> 00:08:59,540
Please allow me
to hold your funeral...

137
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,080
right here.

138
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,250
Wait.

139
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:06,380
Right here?

140
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:09,520
You mean...

141
00:09:09,790 --> 00:09:12,720
I can only leave this place
once I'm dead?

142
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,860
Wouldn't that be a peaceful end?

143
00:09:16,630 --> 00:09:17,630
Well then,

144
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:19,630
I'll see you next time.

145
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:23,070
Right. Take care.

146
00:09:40,450 --> 00:09:42,490
Had my daughter grown up safely,

147
00:09:43,250 --> 00:09:45,190
she'd be exactly this age.

148
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:48,990
Still, we're father and daughter.

149
00:09:49,990 --> 00:09:51,500
Even if we passed each other
on the street,

150
00:09:52,130 --> 00:09:53,800
I'd recognize her instantly,
wouldn't I?

151
00:09:57,900 --> 00:10:00,240
(The Three Women Leading Cheongma)

152
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:22,790
So, he hasn't been causing
any trouble?

153
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:24,060
That's right.

154
00:10:24,130 --> 00:10:26,730
The motel owner is keeping
a close eye on him.

155
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:28,470
He's no simple man.

156
00:10:28,870 --> 00:10:30,700
Right about now,

157
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,240
he's likely racking his brain
to figure out a way to escape.

158
00:10:34,810 --> 00:10:38,610
Having him institutionalized
at the right time seems cleanest.

159
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:42,580
Yes, that would probably be
the safest way to handle him.

160
00:10:43,750 --> 00:10:46,480
Find a facility that's as far away
from Seoul as possible.

161
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:48,020
Understood.

162
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:51,660
Also,

163
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:55,430
it seems Ko Eun Seol
is running around trying to find...

164
00:10:55,490 --> 00:10:56,660
the person who killed Seo Hyun Jae.

165
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:59,230
Shouldn't you look into that?

166
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:03,670
Especially in front of Ko Eun Seol,

167
00:11:03,670 --> 00:11:05,040
make sure you watch your expression.

168
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,840
She's been through thick and thin,
so she can be pretty sharp.

169
00:11:09,470 --> 00:11:10,510
Got it.

170
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:12,540
I'll be careful.

171
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,850
Are there no other opinions?

172
00:11:17,110 --> 00:11:18,620
- No.
- Let's wrap up the meeting then.

173
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:23,220
By the way,
the team has something to tell you.

174
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:25,920
- The team?
- Yes.

175
00:11:27,790 --> 00:11:32,060
We would love to help plan
your engagement party.

176
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:33,400
There's no need for that.

177
00:11:34,070 --> 00:11:36,100
Why would we involve the staff
in a personal matter?

178
00:11:36,630 --> 00:11:39,970
It's not like that.
We really want to help.

179
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:43,210
We consider this separate
from our work.

180
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:47,010
Exactly. We just really want
to congratulate both of you,

181
00:11:47,450 --> 00:11:48,950
so we're offering to help out.

182
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,120
See? You heard them.

183
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:53,920
Ko Eun Seol also agreed to help us
pick out rings.

184
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,490
Right?

185
00:12:00,060 --> 00:12:02,060
Sure, I'll help out.

186
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:04,800
Thank you all so much.

187
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:08,970
Once the engagement ceremony's over,
I'll buy you all a huge dinner.

188
00:12:29,390 --> 00:12:30,420
Hello?

189
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:33,390
Hello, I'm calling
from the Cheongma HR team.

190
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:36,190
Am I speaking
with Mr. Seo Hyun Jae's sister?

191
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,560
Yes, this is she.

192
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:43,230
I'm calling to let you know...

193
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,640
his personal items must be picked up
by the end of the week.

194
00:12:48,610 --> 00:12:50,440
Okay, I'll swing by.

195
00:12:51,210 --> 00:12:52,740
Right, thank you.

196
00:13:08,730 --> 00:13:09,930
Mi Rae, hey.

197
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:14,300
Eun Seol, can I ask you for a favor?

198
00:13:34,490 --> 00:13:36,320
(Head of Legal Affairs)

199
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:15,830
(Eun Seol's Retrial Documents)

200
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:35,850
Hae Ra says we can pick a date
for the engagement,

201
00:14:36,410 --> 00:14:37,780
but is that really okay?

202
00:14:41,050 --> 00:14:42,650
I don't think
that'll be possible right now.

203
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:44,560
I'd like to proceed...

204
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:47,960
only after my mother
fully accepts our engagement.

205
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:49,760
Right, I understand.

206
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,660
But you know,

207
00:14:54,270 --> 00:14:55,930
there's a lot of talk...

208
00:14:56,070 --> 00:14:58,500
going around about you.

209
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,400
They're calling you Cheongma's
unworthy son-in-law,

210
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,040
a charity case, or an adopted son.

211
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:06,810
So the longer this drags on,
the worse it gets for you.

212
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:11,380
Dragging it out like this...

213
00:15:11,450 --> 00:15:13,650
will also reflect poorly
on Cheongma's image.

214
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:17,990
Besides, Hae Ra's clear
that she won't wait any longer.

215
00:15:20,290 --> 00:15:21,460
I'll think about it.

216
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:25,630
How can you possibly cater
to everyone's feelings?

217
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:29,100
You need to know how to ignore them
and just move on.

218
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:33,070
Anyone aiming for greatness
shouldn't dwell on such matters.

219
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:34,840
Right.

220
00:15:36,210 --> 00:15:37,240
Anyway,

221
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:41,210
the engagement will take place
within the month.

222
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:46,150
If you delay it any further,
we'll call the whole thing off.

223
00:15:49,590 --> 00:15:50,590
Understood.

224
00:15:57,590 --> 00:16:00,300
You're here.
What did the police say?

225
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:03,800
I think they'll conclude it was
a crime of impulse.

226
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:10,110
Come sit here.
Have a cup of warm tea first.

227
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:18,850
What's this?

228
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:21,520
It's the road to the warehouse
where he died.

229
00:16:21,850 --> 00:16:22,920
You just never know.

230
00:16:23,450 --> 00:16:25,620
There could be CCTV nearby
that the police missed.

231
00:16:28,330 --> 00:16:31,330
During my mother's case,
that was what I regretted the most.

232
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:33,300
What, exactly?

233
00:16:33,430 --> 00:16:35,270
That I didn't take any action.

234
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:40,500
Being so consumed by grief
that I didn't actively investigate...

235
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:42,070
was my biggest regret.

236
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:45,240
So this time,
I'm going to take action myself.

237
00:16:58,020 --> 00:16:59,460
So, boss,

238
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:01,830
you just focus entirely
on grieving for Attorney Seo.

239
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:04,260
I'll take care of the rest.

240
00:17:05,230 --> 00:17:07,160
Why are you being so good to me?

241
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:08,770
What about the consequences?

242
00:17:10,170 --> 00:17:11,200
I told you.

243
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:15,070
My goal is to be happy
one day at a time.

244
00:17:16,570 --> 00:17:18,640
I'm not going to think about
the distant future right now.

245
00:17:19,510 --> 00:17:20,580
Right now,

246
00:17:20,910 --> 00:17:23,410
all I care about is the Mi Rae
sitting right in front of me.

247
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:27,420
That's the only future
I intend to protect right now.

248
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:47,040
What?

249
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:50,740
A post was uploaded
about Director Oh Tae Seop?

250
00:17:51,410 --> 00:17:54,080
Yes, about
his special recruitment hiring...

251
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:57,180
and the car accident
that happened around then.

252
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:01,020
A car accident?

253
00:18:01,890 --> 00:18:02,890
Yes.

254
00:18:04,390 --> 00:18:05,490
Who posted it?

255
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:07,660
We tracked the IP address,

256
00:18:08,190 --> 00:18:10,190
and it came from an internet cafe
out in the provinces.

257
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:12,500
Did you immediately delete the post?

258
00:18:13,030 --> 00:18:15,300
Yes, luckily,
we managed to take it down...

259
00:18:15,370 --> 00:18:16,600
as soon as it was posted.

260
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,300
Well, for special hires,

261
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:21,940
this kind of thing happens
all the time.

262
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:26,180
Can I take a look
at that deleted post?

263
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:28,810
Yes, I'll send it to you right away.

264
00:18:37,190 --> 00:18:39,920
The engagement will take place
within the month.

265
00:18:41,490 --> 00:18:44,730
If you delay it any further,
we'll call the whole thing off.

266
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:52,970
Seok Jin, let's go get
our engagement rings this weekend.

267
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:58,740
Okay.

268
00:18:58,910 --> 00:19:00,610
We'll pick a date
for the ceremony too.

269
00:19:08,090 --> 00:19:11,360
(Coloring Book)

270
00:19:17,730 --> 00:19:20,700
Nice lady,
I finished the coloring book.

271
00:19:21,630 --> 00:19:23,600
I'd love to show it to you.

272
00:19:38,650 --> 00:19:39,920
Attorney Seo,

273
00:19:41,490 --> 00:19:44,020
what on earth were you looking for?

274
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:48,890
When we had dinner
with the directors that day,

275
00:19:50,190 --> 00:19:53,600
you went to check
on my husband's situation.

276
00:19:54,830 --> 00:19:56,070
Yes, I did.

277
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:58,900
And he was sitting alone
in the restaurant?

278
00:20:00,170 --> 00:20:02,170
I thought he had already left,

279
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:04,740
so I was surprised
to see him still there.

280
00:20:05,010 --> 00:20:08,180
Then you two must've had dinner
alone that night.

281
00:20:09,310 --> 00:20:10,910
Did you mention that to me?

282
00:20:12,250 --> 00:20:13,280
Sorry?

283
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:15,120
I told you...

284
00:20:15,850 --> 00:20:18,260
not to be alone with my husband.

285
00:20:21,690 --> 00:20:22,860
I'm sorry,

286
00:20:23,190 --> 00:20:25,400
- but the situation that night...
- I know.

287
00:20:25,430 --> 00:20:27,260
It couldn't be helped.

288
00:20:27,330 --> 00:20:30,630
If so, you should've told me.
Aren't I right, Director Joo?

289
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:34,670
- I'm sorry.
- Forget it.

290
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:37,710
Be more careful from now on.

291
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:43,050
You know I have an appointment
with Ms. Yang today, right?

292
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:47,650
If you've got time, Director Joo,
join me.

293
00:20:48,550 --> 00:20:51,360
Ms. Yang actually asked
how you were doing.

294
00:20:51,390 --> 00:20:52,390
Is that okay?

295
00:20:52,490 --> 00:20:54,290
Sure, I'll join you.

296
00:21:12,110 --> 00:21:14,610
Did you get home safely that day?

297
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:17,180
Yes.

298
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:19,720
You got home safely too, right?

299
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:23,050
You looked a bit tipsy.

300
00:21:24,620 --> 00:21:26,990
It was one of those days
I just wanted to get wasted,

301
00:21:29,030 --> 00:21:30,530
but I couldn't even manage that.

302
00:21:31,060 --> 00:21:32,130
I see.

303
00:21:35,930 --> 00:21:38,170
There's a restaurant
Attorney Seo and I used to go to,

304
00:21:39,270 --> 00:21:41,270
but I don't think I can face
going back there anytime soon.

305
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:45,140
We always ate lunch together.

306
00:21:48,710 --> 00:21:51,210
You can go with me from now on.

307
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:54,220
No.

308
00:21:55,290 --> 00:21:56,750
I want to be alone for now.

309
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:12,800
Director Joo, it's been a while,
and you look completely different.

310
00:22:13,970 --> 00:22:16,270
Are you seeing someone?

311
00:22:17,770 --> 00:22:18,840
No, ma'am.

312
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:21,210
Now's not the time for that.

313
00:22:21,210 --> 00:22:23,010
As if there's a good or bad time
for dating.

314
00:22:23,150 --> 00:22:24,610
If there's chemistry, you date.

315
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:27,420
Of course,
Director Joo can date too.

316
00:22:28,450 --> 00:22:30,620
Are there any good men around?

317
00:22:30,950 --> 00:22:33,460
What's your type, Director Joo?

318
00:22:34,490 --> 00:22:37,160
Someone reliable like CEO Kang?

319
00:22:39,330 --> 00:22:40,560
No, I...

320
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:42,270
Please look into this, Ms. Yang,

321
00:22:42,570 --> 00:22:45,070
and find a suitable partner
for Director Joo.

322
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:46,800
She should also experience...

323
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:49,970
being truly loved by a man.

324
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:53,380
That's not hard to do.

325
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:57,950
Director Joo, I'll send you
a few photos right now,

326
00:22:58,280 --> 00:22:59,280
so take a look.

327
00:23:13,530 --> 00:23:16,630
Unbelievable.
Are they messing with me?

328
00:23:17,630 --> 00:23:20,940
Fine, I'll happily play along.

329
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:24,340
Just wait and see.
I'll have a lot of fun...

330
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:27,040
playing with your husband.

331
00:23:28,550 --> 00:23:30,380
You messed with the wrong person.

332
00:23:32,150 --> 00:23:34,890
Director, I need your help.

333
00:23:36,220 --> 00:23:37,220
With what?

334
00:23:37,590 --> 00:23:40,420
I'm looking at necklaces
as a gift for Ms. Park.

335
00:23:41,020 --> 00:23:42,030
Which one should I get?

336
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:44,290
Just go with any of those options.

337
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:48,200
Have you still not figured out
So Yeon's taste?

338
00:23:48,830 --> 00:23:50,400
Did something happen, Director?

339
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:53,800
No, it's nothing.
I'll go over them later.

340
00:23:54,810 --> 00:23:56,670
- I'll leave this here.
- Okay.

341
00:24:12,490 --> 00:24:15,890
It's me. Upload that post once more.

342
00:24:23,630 --> 00:24:25,640
Oh, hey. Nice lady!

343
00:24:26,740 --> 00:24:28,310
Have you been well?

344
00:24:28,540 --> 00:24:32,340
Yes. Nice lady, sit here.
Right over here.

345
00:24:32,780 --> 00:24:35,410
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

346
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:40,720
Yes, Auntie.

347
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:42,420
Seok Jin, I'm sorry,

348
00:24:42,850 --> 00:24:46,690
but something came up today
and I can't pick up your mom.

349
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:48,290
Is that so?

350
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:50,530
I'll go to her.
Where's my mother right now?

351
00:25:01,370 --> 00:25:02,910
Nice lady, hold on.

352
00:25:04,040 --> 00:25:05,610
Did something happen?

353
00:25:06,580 --> 00:25:08,280
You look sad.

354
00:25:14,120 --> 00:25:15,190
Is it...

355
00:25:15,290 --> 00:25:16,420
that obvious?

356
00:25:17,190 --> 00:25:18,190
Yes.

357
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:21,590
Actually...

358
00:25:23,860 --> 00:25:25,260
Actually, not too long ago,

359
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:29,830
someone very precious to me...

360
00:25:31,470 --> 00:25:32,800
passed away.

361
00:25:36,940 --> 00:25:38,480
I see.

362
00:25:39,780 --> 00:25:43,080
That must be why you're so sad.

363
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:53,460
I'll give you a hug.

364
00:25:56,130 --> 00:25:57,190
You see,

365
00:25:58,430 --> 00:26:01,230
on the day my husband passed,

366
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:06,900
I held Seok Jin tightly...

367
00:26:07,840 --> 00:26:09,310
just like this.

368
00:26:27,060 --> 00:26:28,120
Let's go.

369
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:32,760
I'll take you home.

370
00:26:35,230 --> 00:26:36,870
Mr. Seok Jin.

371
00:26:39,670 --> 00:26:40,670
No, thank you.

372
00:26:41,500 --> 00:26:42,770
I'll get going first.

373
00:26:43,540 --> 00:26:45,440
Mother, I'll see you around.

374
00:26:45,540 --> 00:26:47,340
What? Wait.

375
00:26:48,210 --> 00:26:51,480
Nice lady, you should come with us.

376
00:26:57,550 --> 00:26:58,560
Let's go, Mom.

377
00:27:02,790 --> 00:27:04,730
This is for my husband, right?

378
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:07,700
I'll handle it.
You can call it a night.

379
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:14,800
Seriously...

380
00:27:17,540 --> 00:27:18,540
Director.

381
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:20,110
Hey.

382
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,380
Try this.

383
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:23,680
What is it?

384
00:27:24,150 --> 00:27:25,680
Lately, you've been
getting hot flashes...

385
00:27:25,780 --> 00:27:27,120
and having trouble
sleeping at night.

386
00:27:27,450 --> 00:27:30,390
Having such severe mood swings
are all symptoms of menopause.

387
00:27:30,820 --> 00:27:33,260
Taking one packet of this a day
is really good for you.

388
00:27:34,320 --> 00:27:36,360
So you brought this for me?

389
00:27:37,290 --> 00:27:40,130
No wonder I've been so moody lately,

390
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:43,200
tossing and turning at night
and drained all day.

391
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:47,470
Of course. I brought it to help
with your menopause.

392
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:50,440
You know how precious
you are to me, Director.

393
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:54,710
Right, thanks.

394
00:27:55,180 --> 00:27:58,050
Thanks to you,
I'll sleep well tonight.

395
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:08,560
This is good.

396
00:28:10,230 --> 00:28:12,700
You'll help me choose a gift
for Ms. Park, won't you?

397
00:28:13,130 --> 00:28:14,860
All right. I'll help you.

398
00:28:55,340 --> 00:28:56,440
Director Joo,

399
00:28:57,370 --> 00:28:58,610
what are you still doing up?

400
00:29:02,050 --> 00:29:05,010
I thought you would be troubled
after seeing the post.

401
00:29:07,880 --> 00:29:09,250
Tell me about it.

402
00:29:10,320 --> 00:29:12,620
Who on earth keeps posting
things like this?

403
00:29:13,390 --> 00:29:16,030
It's likely someone
from the Cheongma logistics center,

404
00:29:16,260 --> 00:29:18,500
where Director Oh Tae Seop
used to work.

405
00:29:18,630 --> 00:29:22,300
Track down that IP address,
and make sure you find this jerk.

406
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,670
Yes, I'll do that.

407
00:29:31,540 --> 00:29:32,540
Sir.

408
00:29:34,310 --> 00:29:36,550
It's about Director Oh Tae Seop.

409
00:29:39,620 --> 00:29:42,550
What's his connection
to Chief Cha's father?

410
00:29:45,050 --> 00:29:47,860
The last time
I went to So Yeon's house,

411
00:29:47,890 --> 00:29:49,160
we talked about the accident,

412
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:52,000
and I heard Oh Tae Seop's name.

413
00:29:53,900 --> 00:29:55,100
According to So Yeon,

414
00:29:55,770 --> 00:29:57,170
a man named Oh Tae Seop...

415
00:29:57,370 --> 00:30:00,200
was behind the accident
involving Chief Cha's father.

416
00:30:00,570 --> 00:30:02,570
What are you talking about?

417
00:30:04,170 --> 00:30:07,140
Director Joo,
what are you imagining right now?

418
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:09,950
Would I have brought
such a person into Cheongma?

419
00:30:09,950 --> 00:30:11,180
The man who killed my friend?

420
00:30:19,390 --> 00:30:20,790
It's okay, sir.

421
00:30:22,830 --> 00:30:25,860
You don't have to hide anything
from me.

422
00:30:33,970 --> 00:30:36,710
You must've been so lonely
all these years.

423
00:30:38,070 --> 00:30:41,480
I want to ease
that emotional burden of yours, sir.

424
00:30:42,850 --> 00:30:44,150
No matter what happens,

425
00:30:44,880 --> 00:30:47,120
I will always be on your side.

426
00:30:50,990 --> 00:30:52,090
Director Joo...

427
00:31:31,830 --> 00:31:35,500
(A Trap Called Desire)

428
00:31:35,770 --> 00:31:38,970
He said he'd help both you and me.

429
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:42,270
What message was he trying to send
with those items?

430
00:31:42,610 --> 00:31:44,770
Maybe she can go back
to how she used to be.

431
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:47,580
I mean So Yeon's memories,
from before the accident.

432
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:50,410
I feel like I'll spend my whole life
waiting on Ms. Park.

433
00:31:50,480 --> 00:31:51,580
With a mother-in-law like her,

434
00:31:51,580 --> 00:31:53,250
it'd be better to have
no in-laws at all.

435
00:31:53,250 --> 00:31:56,020
There is someone else
who is truly terrifying.

436
00:31:56,190 --> 00:31:57,490
Our scholarship program?

437
00:31:57,490 --> 00:32:00,390
Shouldn't you understand the work
before asking for reports?

438
00:32:00,490 --> 00:32:02,730
Why would I die at your hands?

439
00:32:03,130 --> 00:32:04,390
Just wait until I find my daughter.

440
00:32:04,930 --> 00:32:07,030
Joo Hye Sung, just you wait.

441
00:32:07,960 --> 00:32:09,970
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
